# [[.Title]]

A Steward plugin for [[.Title]], built with [`@treno-dev/steward-sdk`](https://github.com/treno-dev/steward-sdk/tree/main/js).

## Run

```sh
npm install
steward plugin validate node src/plugin.ts
```

Node runs `src/plugin.ts` directly. A plugin is started by a runner, not by hand: run directly it says so
and exits. Use `steward plugin validate` to check it, and
`steward plugin run --context context.json node src/plugin.ts` to invoke it. Write logs to standard error.

Run `npm run check` to type-check.

## Where things are

`src/plugin.ts` declares the integration (what it needs to connect), each kind of resource and the
handlers Steward calls: `provision`, `deprovision`, `grantAccess`, `revokeAccess` and `getAccess`.
Each handler is annotated with the request and response types the SDK exports. Delete the handlers
you do not need: Steward offers only what you implement.

To add a kind of resource, call `plugin.resource({ kind, ... })` again with its own inputs, outputs and
handlers.

See the [SDK README](https://github.com/treno-dev/steward-sdk/blob/main/js/README.md) for
everything a plugin can declare.
